      "originalLine": 57,
      "title": "Pin the byte-hashed source closure to LF",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Pin the byte-hashed source closure to LF**\n\nOn a checkout where these newly included modules have CRLF line endings, `visit()` reads them as text and hashes the newline-normalized `source.encode()`, while `verify_packaged()` and `capture_capability_operator()` later hash the raw bytes. The new paths are not pinned with `text eol=lf` in `.gitattributes`; converting only `discovery-lab.mjs` to CRLF reproduces a manifest digest that differs from the source file, causing validation and release packaging to fail on such checkouts. Pin every closure member to LF or compute the catalogue digest from the same raw bytes the validators use.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "classification": "New exact24d configured-review finding; not a moved historical original-commit comment.",
      "independentlyReproducedByThisMonitor": false
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "id": 4345508855,
      "reviewId": 5610481904,
      "url": "https://github.com/MontrealAI/AGI-Alpha-Agent-v0/pull/4851#discussion_r4345508855",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T07:12:28Z",
