      "commit": "24d58598f896106323f2c120487586bdf5104612",
      "originalCommit": "24d58598f896106323f2c120487586bdf5104612",
      "path": "examples/successor-capability/discovery-lab-reproduce.mjs",
      "line": 18,
      "startLine": 17,
      "originalLine": 18,
      "title": "Resolve symlinks before enforcing output isolation",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve symlinks before enforcing output isolation**\n\nAlthough the workflow now supplies `runner.temp`, the CLI's remaining boundary check is lexical: if an apparently external path such as `/tmp/evidence` is a symlink to a directory inside the repository, `relative()` begins with `..` and passes, but `mkdirSync()` and the later writes follow the symlink into the checkout. This defeats the explicit outside-repository guarantee and can contaminate or overwrite checkout evidence; resolve the existing output or its nearest existing parent to its real path before applying the boundary test.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "classification": "New exact24d configured-review finding; not a moved historical original-commit comment.",
      "independentlyReproducedByThisMonitor": false
    }
